Setting Up Prometheus Monitoring for Argo CD
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Install and configure Prometheus monitoring system in Kubernetes
Set up Prometheus to collect metrics from Argo CD applications
Configure ServiceMonitor resources for Argo CD monitoring
Access and interpret Prometheus metrics dashboard
Understand the integration between Prometheus and Argo CD for comprehensive application monitoring
Troubleshoot common monitoring setup issues
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Kubernetes concepts (pods, services, deployments)
Familiarity with YAML configuration files
Knowledge of Argo CD fundamentals from previous labs
Understanding of monitoring concepts and metrics
Experience with command-line interface operations
Lab Environment
Al Nafi provides Linux-based cloud machines for this lab. Simply click Start Lab to access your dedicated environment. The provided Linux machine is bare metal with no pre-installed tools, so you will install all required components during the lab exercises.

